E('wheel|invention of the wheel', 'The wheel is one of humanity’s most important inventions.', 'It was invented in Mesopotamia around 3500 BC.', 'It was first used for pottery, then carts.', 'Spoked wheels came later, around 2000 BC.', 'Some ancient American cultures used wheels only on toys.', 'It transformed transport and machinery.')
E('writing|invention of writing|cuneiform|hieroglyphs', 'Writing was invented independently in several places.', 'The earliest known writing appeared in Mesopotamia around 3200 BC.', 'Sumerian cuneiform began as a way to keep accounts.', 'Egyptian hieroglyphs appeared around the same time.', 'Writing also developed in China and Mesoamerica.', 'The alphabet developed around 1800 BC and was spread by the Phoenicians.')
E('paper|invention of paper|cai lun', 'Paper was invented in China.', 'Cai Lun, an imperial official, is credited with improving it around AD 105.', 'It was made from bark, hemp and rags.', 'Knowledge of papermaking spread to the Islamic world in the 8th century.', 'It reached Europe by the 11th century.', 'It made books and records far cheaper.')
E('gunpowder', 'Gunpowder was invented in China.', 'It was discovered around the 9th century.', 'Chinese alchemists found it while searching for an elixir of life.', 'It is a mix of saltpetre, charcoal and sulphur.', 'It was used in fireworks and weapons.', 'It transformed warfare worldwide.')
E('compass|magnetic compass', 'The magnetic compass was invented in China.', 'It was used for navigation by the 11th century.', 'Early compasses used magnetised needles or lodestone.', 'It spread to Europe and the Islamic world.', 'It made long ocean voyages possible.')
E('telescope', 'The telescope was invented in the Netherlands.', 'Hans Lippershey applied for a patent in 1608.', 'Galileo built improved versions in 1609.', 'Newton built the first practical reflecting telescope in 1668.', 'Telescopes revealed moons, galaxies and the expanding universe.')
E('radio|marconi|guglielmo marconi', 'Radio uses electromagnetic waves to send sound without wires.', 'Guglielmo Marconi sent the first transatlantic radio signal in 1901.', 'Others, including Tesla and Popov, made key contributions.', 'Radio broadcasting began in the 1920s.', 'Radio helped save survivors of the Titanic.', 'It brought news and music into homes worldwide.')
E('television|tv|john logie baird', 'Television transmits moving images and sound.', 'John Logie Baird demonstrated a working television in 1926.', 'Philo Farnsworth developed an all-electronic system.', 'TV became common in homes in the 1950s.', 'Colour TV spread in the 1960s.', 'It transformed entertainment, news and politics.')
E('car|automobile|first car|history of the car', 'The automobile changed how people travel.', 'Karl Benz built the first practical petrol-powered car in 1885 and patented it in 1886.', 'His wife Bertha made the first long-distance car journey in 1888.', 'Henry Ford’s Model T made cars affordable.', 'Electric cars have grown rapidly in the 21st century.')
E('airplane|aeroplane|aircraft|plane', 'Airplanes are powered aircraft with fixed wings.', 'The Wright brothers made the first powered flight in 1903.', 'Aircraft were used in the First World War.', 'Jet engines were developed in the 1930s.', 'Commercial air travel became common after the 1950s.', 'Concorde flew faster than sound from 1976 to 2003.')
E('electricity', 'Electricity is the flow of electric charge.', 'It was studied seriously from the 18th century.', 'Benjamin Franklin showed lightning is electrical.', 'Alessandro Volta built the first battery in 1800.', 'Faraday discovered how to generate it with magnets.', 'Edison and Tesla helped bring it into homes.')
E('smartphone|mobile phone|cell phone', 'Mobile phones let people talk without wires.', 'The first handheld mobile call was made by Martin Cooper of Motorola in 1973.', 'Early mobile phones were large and expensive.', 'Text messaging began in the 1990s.', 'The iPhone, launched in 2007, popularised smartphones.', 'Billions of people now carry one.')
E('photography|camera|first photograph', 'Photography captures images using light.', 'The oldest surviving photograph was taken by Nicéphore Niépce around 1826.', 'It needed an exposure of hours.', 'Louis Daguerre developed the daguerreotype in 1839.', 'Kodak made cameras easy for everyone from 1888.', 'Digital cameras replaced film in the 2000s.')
E('vaccine history|first vaccine', 'The first vaccine was developed by Edward Jenner in 1796.', 'It protected against smallpox.', 'Louis Pasteur later made vaccines for rabies and anthrax.', 'The polio vaccine was developed by Jonas Salk in the 1950s.', 'Vaccines have saved hundreds of millions of lives.')
E('jonas salk|polio|polio vaccine', 'Jonas Salk was an American researcher who developed the first successful polio vaccine.', 'It was announced in 1955.', 'Polio paralysed many children.', 'Salk did not patent the vaccine.', 'Asked who owned it, he said, “Could you patent the sun?”', 'Polio is now close to eradication.')
E('artificial intelligence|ai history|machine learning', 'Artificial intelligence is the science of making machines that can perform tasks needing intelligence.', 'The term was coined at a conference at Dartmouth College in 1956.', 'Alan Turing proposed the Turing test in 1950.', 'IBM’s Deep Blue beat world chess champion Garry Kasparov in 1997.', 'Machine learning lets computers learn patterns from data.', 'Large language models became widely used in the 2020s.')
